.TH BENCHMARK\-NETWORK\-PTS 1 "February 2026" "benchmarking" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
benchmark\-network\-pts.sh \- benchmark network performance using the Phoronix Test Suite
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B benchmark\-network\-pts.sh
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B benchmark\-network\-pts.sh
\fB\-\-server\-mode\fR
[\fB\-\-interface\fR \fIIFACE\fR|\fIIP\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Benchmarks network performance across three modes.
.PP
.B Standalone
tests always run on a single host and require no second machine:
.RS
.TP
.B pts/network\-loopback
TCP stack throughput through the loopback interface (kernel buffer performance).
.TP
.B pts/sockperf
Socket API latency (ping-pong, under-load) and throughput; starts its own
server process locally.
.RE
.PP
.B Peer
tests require a second host running the script in
.B \-\-server\-mode
and are enabled by supplying
.BR \-\-server :
.RS
.TP
.B pts/iperf
TCP bulk throughput (single and multi-stream scaled to NIC line rate) and UDP throughput.
.TP
.B pts/netperf
TCP/UDP throughput in both directions and request-response latency.
.RE
.PP
.B Server mode
(\fB\-\-server\-mode\fR) installs the test binaries via PTS on the remote host, then
starts
.B iperf3
and
.B netserver
as local daemons.
Stop the daemons with Ctrl\-C when the benchmark run is complete.
.PP
Parallel stream count and UDP target bandwidth scale automatically with NIC line
rate (e.g.\& 25 streams on 25\ GbE, 100 streams on 100\ GbE).
Override with \fB\-\-streams\fR or supply the speed manually with \fB\-\-nic\-speed\fR
for virtual NICs that do not expose speed via sysfs.
.PP
Before peer tests the script computes the bandwidth-delay product (BDP) for the
link and warns if TCP socket buffer sizes are too small to saturate the pipe.
.PP
PTS is installed automatically on supported distributions (Ubuntu, Debian,
Rocky Linux, openSUSE) if not already present.
.PP
Results are collected into
.B ./benchmark\-results/<result\-id>/
relative to the directory from which the script is invoked.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-server " " \fIADDRESS\fR
IP address or hostname of the peer for
.B pts/iperf
and
.B pts/netperf
tests.
When omitted, only standalone tests are run.
Mutually exclusive with \fB\-\-server\-mode\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-server\-mode
Start
.B iperf3
and
.B netserver
as local server daemons.
Installs test binaries via PTS if not already installed.
Mutually exclusive with \fB\-\-server\fR.
.TP
.BR \-I ", " \-\-interface " " \fIIFACE\fR|\fIIP\fR
In client mode: egress interface used for NIC speed detection.
In server mode: interface name or IP address to bind the daemons to.
Omit to bind to all interfaces (server) or auto-detect (client).
.TP
.B \-\-nic\-speed " " \fIMbps\fR
Override the NIC line rate in Mbps (e.g.\&
.B 100000
for 100\ GbE).
Client mode only.
Useful for virtual NICs that do not expose speed via sysfs.
.TP
.B \-\-streams " " \fIN\fR
Override the parallel stream count for
.B pts/iperf
multi-stream tests.
Client mode only.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-upload
Upload results to OpenBenchmarking.org after the run completes.
Requires \fB\-\-result\-id\fR and \fB\-\-result\-name\fR.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-result\-id " " \fIID\fR
Short identifier for the run (e.g.\&
.IR dc1\-vm1\-to\-vm2 ).
Used as the output directory name, the PTS result name prefix, and the upload
identifier on OpenBenchmarking.org.
Default: auto-generated timestamp string.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-result\-name " " \fINAME\fR
Human-readable display name for the result (e.g.\&
.IR "VM1 to VM2 \- 100GbE vSwitch" ).
Required when \fB\-\-upload\fR is specified.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display a help message and exit.
.SH OUTPUT
.TP
.B ./benchmark\-results/<result\-id>/<result\-id>\-system\-snapshot.txt
System snapshot captured before the run.
.TP
.BI ./benchmark\-results/<result\-id>/<result\-id>_ test\-variant /
One PTS result directory per test variant (e.g.\&
.BR <result\-id>_network\-loopback/ ,
.BR <result\-id>_sockperf/ ,
.BR <result\-id>_iperf_tcp_1stream/ ,
\&...).
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Start server daemons on the remote host, bound to a specific interface:
.PP
.nf
.RS
\&./benchmark\-network\-pts.sh \-\-server\-mode \-\-interface eth0
.RE
.fi
.PP
Run standalone tests only (no second machine needed):
.PP
.nf
.RS
\&./benchmark\-network\-pts.sh
.RE
.fi
.PP
Run the full suite against a peer:
.PP
.nf
.RS
\&./benchmark\-network\-pts.sh \-\-server 192.168.100.10 \\
    \-\-result\-id "dc1\-vm1\-to\-vm2" \\
    \-\-result\-name "VM1 to VM2 \- Ceph cluster network"
.RE
.fi
.PP
100\ GbE link where the virtual NIC does not report speed via sysfs:
.PP
.nf
.RS
\&./benchmark\-network\-pts.sh \-\-server 192.168.100.10 \\
    \-\-interface eth0 \-\-nic\-speed 100000 \\
    \-\-result\-id "dc1\-vm1\-to\-vm2" \\
    \-\-result\-name "VM1 to VM2 \- 100GbE vSwitch"
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR benchmark\-cpu\-pts.sh (1),
.BR benchmark\-memory\-pts.sh (1),
.BR benchmark\-storage\-pts.sh (1),
